    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BWDp9cgemxzr2hZ9jvXJcG)_\n\nFollow-up to #480 (merged): `citar-open` still showed `Updating bibliography`.\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Base: `main`; no dependency. Touches only `sp-citations` (`.el`, its section in `sp-academic.org`, the preload test).\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-d7whd6`, not number-prefixed: a cloud session cannot rename a branch after the PR number is known.\n\n## Likely cause (from reading the code; not confirmed on your Emacs)\n\n- `citar` keeps, with each file, the list of fields it parsed (`citar--fields-to-parse`) and reads the file again when the list differs.\n- The list comes from the templates, and `sp-citations--layout-templates` only adds `${tags keywords:N}` when the room is 110 columns or more. So the list depended on the width of the frame.\n- The preload ran at one width and the first call at another (the posframe takes a fraction of the frame), so the cache was thrown away.\n- Other possible causes (preload not finished yet, not in the cache) are not excluded: see `sp-citations-preload-explain` below.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `sp-citations--stable-fields`, a filter on `citar--fields-to-parse`: sorts the list and always has `tags` and `keywords` in it, so it is the same at any width.\n- `M-x sp-citations-preload-explain`: for each file, says whether it is in the cache, tied to `global`, has the same fields and size, and whether the preload is still waiting. If it still reads a file again, run it before `citar-open` and send me the text.\n- The end of a pass says `citar preload: N bibliography file(s) ready` in `*Messages*`.\n- The disk cache from before this change has the old fields, so each file is parsed once more after updating.\n- Docs as bullets; no CHANGELOG edit; no `when-let`.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `tests/sp-citations-preload-test.el`: 13 tests pass on Emacs 29.3 (stand-in for `citar-cache`), including that the fields are equal with and without the tags column, and the explain command. `tests/sp-citations-layout-test.el`: 13 pass.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh`: the `.el` is what the doc tangles to.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Nothing ran against the real `citar` or your bibliography, so the width explanation is a reading of the code, not a reproduction.\n- Whether the preload finished before your first `citar-open`: it waits for 3 idle seconds, then reads one file per idle pause.\n- Whether `citar--fields-to-parse` is used elsewhere in your citar version in a way that needs the original order.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin claude/project-thread-d7whd6; git checkout claude/project-thread-d7whd6`, restart Emacs\n- [ ] Wait until `*Messages*` says `citar preload: N bibliography file(s) ready`\n- [ ] `M-x sp-citations-preload-explain`: every file says `ready`\n- [ ] `M-x citar-open`: no `Updating bibliography` line, no wait\n- [ ] Resize the frame (or toggle the posframe), `M-x citar-open` again: still no `Updating`\n- [ ] Quit and restart: the first pass after the restart parses nothing (the disk cache is used)\n- [ ] If a file still re-reads: run `M-x sp-citations-preload-explain` before `citar-open` and send the text\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main && git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs.\n- Delete `citar-bibliography.eld` in your cache dir for a cold start.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCyfpEM7dFcJmFXN4v)_",
